From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:48:36 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] nfc: nxp-nci: do not hold info_lock across
 nci_unregister_device()

nxp_nci_remove() takes info_lock and then calls nci_unregister_device().
If the device is up, nci_unregister_device() closes it through
nci_close_device() and the driver's close hook, nxp_nci_close(), which
takes info_lock again. The mutex is not recursive, so removing a powered
device hangs: the unbind or rmmod never returns, and a later shutdown
blocks in device_shutdown().

Seen on a Pixel 9a whose NFC controller is driven through this I2C
transport: with the controller powered by neard, the device's removal
during a suspend attempt hung with nxp_nci_close() under
nxp_nci_remove().

Unregister first, outside the lock, then put the chip in cold mode under
the lock, and free the device last.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c b/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c
index 448e5a4e7..386dcd4ff 100644
--- a/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c
+++ b/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/core.c
@@ -186,15 +186,18 @@ void nxp_nci_remove(struct nci_dev *ndev)
 		nxp_nci_fw_work_complete(info, -ESHUTDOWN);
 	cancel_work_sync(&info->fw_info.work);
 
-	mutex_lock(&info->info_lock);
+	/*
+	 * nci_unregister_device() closes an open device through
+	 * nxp_nci_close(), which takes info_lock itself: unregister first.
+	 */
+	nci_unregister_device(ndev);
 
+	mutex_lock(&info->info_lock);
 	if (info->phy_ops->set_mode)
 		info->phy_ops->set_mode(info->phy_id, NXP_NCI_MODE_COLD);
+	mutex_unlock(&info->info_lock);
 
-	nci_unregister_device(ndev);
 	nci_free_device(ndev);
-
-	mutex_unlock(&info->info_lock);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(nxp_nci_remove);
 
